    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Gran-Gran just entered (summoning sick) and o3 Tactic has 6 lands but only 2 Map tokens as other non-land permanents. Using Get Lost on Gran-Gran gives the opponent two additional Map tokens (now 4 total), which provide significant card selection via explore. Meanwhile, Grk41F Memoir has Kaito in hand - a much more powerful threat that could be deployed this turn (4 mana available) and would pressure o3 Tactic's planeswalker-light board. Kaito's hexproof during your turn makes it hard to remove, and its 0 ability with surveil + card draw is a strong engine. Playing Kaito first and saving Get Lost for a more impactful target (or using it later when the Map token downside matters less relative to the threat) seems preferable. The two extra Map tokens given to an Izzet spells deck with Stormchaser's Talent in the graveyard is a real cost.",
