      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Kaito, Bane of Nightmares has 8 loyalty counters. During your turn, he is a 3/4 Ninja creature with hexproof. The opponent is at 5 life. Even if there are no other creatures, Kaito alone attacks for 3 damage (or more with emblems from his +1 ability). But critically, the player chose to skip the attack phase entirely ('skip attack') while the opponent is at 5 life. With Kaito as a 3/4 creature during your turn, attacking would deal at least 3 damage, putting the opponent to 2. Additionally, the Stormchaser's Talent on the battlefield suggests there may be an Otter token (from level 1 entering), though the board doesn't explicitly show one. Regardless, not attacking with Kaito when the opponent is at 5 life is a massive missed opportunity - the opponent could stabilize or find answers. The player's own commentary mentions 'charging into combat with Kaito's colossal frame' but then actually skips the attack.",
